# Push when reasonable

Do **not** wait for the user to ask before pushing. After local commits that are ready to share, push to `origin` when it is reasonable.

## When to push (do it)

- Overnight / harness ticks after a versioned ship commit (`v0.1.x`)
- A coherent feature, fix, or refactor set is committed and builds
- User said to push, or previously asked for unattended push discipline
- Branch is ahead of `origin` and the work is not an unfinished experiment

Prefer: commit → (install/verify if runtime) → **`git push -u origin HEAD`** (or `git push origin <branch>`).

## When not to push

- Secrets, credentials, or `.env` in the commit
- Broken `cargo check` / known red build
- Explicit user “local only” / “don’t push yet”
- Rewriting history that would need force-push to `main`/`master` (never force-push those unless the user explicitly demands it)

## Releases

Do **not** wait for the user to ask. Cut a GitHub Release when the product has
moved on meaningfully from **GitHub Latest**:

- Prefer `python3 scripts/maybe_cut_github_release.py` (gates: ~20+ patches, or
  ≥7 days with ≥5 patches; once per day; clean `main`)
- Overnight ~23:00 flush runs that script after `overnight_git_flush.py`
- Agents may also run it after a coherent ship when Latest is stale
- Tag = `Cargo.toml` version (`v0.1.x`); CI attaches the DMG
- Homebrew cask SHA update is a follow-up after the asset exists
  (`print-release-checksums.sh` → `Casks/mac-stats.rb` → `sync-homebrew-tap.sh`)

Skip only when: secrets in the tree, red build, explicit “local only”, or Latest
already matches `Cargo.toml`.

## Commits

Still follow normal commit hygiene (no `Co-authored-by` / agent attribution). When a task is **finished**, commit and push without waiting to be asked — see `.cursor/rules/no-uncommitted-leftovers.mdc`. Nightly ~23:00 harness flush is a backstop only.
